# Styling Guidelines

## Approach

- Use regular CSS (`.css` files) for component styling; **no inline styles**.
- One `.css` file per component; import as side-effect: `import './Component.css'`.
- Follow BEM methodology with `aceui-` prefix for all class names.
- Use design tokens (CSS variables) for all values; avoid hardcoded colors/sizes.

## Design Tokens

Design tokens are defined in `demo/src/design-tokens.css` and shared with the demo app. Components reference these CSS variables; consumers must ensure tokens are available (e.g. import `design-tokens.css` or provide their own). Use CSS variables instead of hardcoded values.

## CSS Variable Naming

### Colors

#### Global Colors
- `--color-background`: Main background color
- `--color-foreground`: Main text/foreground color
- `--color-focus`: Focus ring color
- `--color-overlay`: Overlay background color

#### Semantic Colors
- Base: `--color-{semantic}` (e.g., `--color-primary`)
- Foreground: `--color-{semantic}-foreground`
- Shades: `--color-{semantic}-{50-900}` (e.g., `--color-primary-500`)
- Semantics: `default`, `primary`, `secondary`, `success`, `warning`, `danger`
- Each semantic color has shades from 50 (lightest) to 900 (darkest)

### Sizing
- Font sizes: `--font-size-tiny`, `--font-size-small`, `--font-size-medium`, `--font-size-large`
- Line heights: `--line-height-tiny`, `--line-height-small`, `--line-height-medium`, `--line-height-large`
- Border radius: `--radius-small`, `--radius-medium`, `--radius-large`
- Border widths: `--border-width-small`, `--border-width-medium`, `--border-width-large`
- Box shadows: `--box-shadow-small`, `--box-shadow-medium`, `--box-shadow-large`

### Other
- Opacity: `--disabled-opacity`, `--hover-opacity`

## BEM (Block Element Modifier) Methodology

Use BEM for class naming with `aceui-` prefix:
- **Block:** standalone component — `aceui-` + kebab-case (`.aceui-button`, `.aceui-modal`). Must be meaningful on its own and reusable.
- **Element:** structural part of a block — double underscore `__` (`.aceui-button__icon`, `.aceui-modal__header`). Describes **what it is**, not how it looks.
- **Modifier:** variant or state — double dash `--` (`.aceui-button--primary`, `.aceui-modal__footer--sticky`). Optional, never structural.

### Examples
- `.aceui-dropdown`, `.aceui-dropdown__menu`, `.aceui-dropdown__item`, `.aceui-dropdown__item--active`
- Block modifier: `.aceui-button .aceui-button--primary .aceui-button--disabled`
- Element modifier: `.aceui-modal__footer .aceui-modal__footer--compact`

### Golden rule
- Can exist alone → **Block**
- Is a part of something → **Element**
- Changes appearance or behavior → **Modifier**

### Elements are one level deep
- Do not nest elements: `.aceui-form__field__label` ❌
- Use flat elements: `.aceui-form__field`, `.aceui-form__label` ✅

### Modifiers must not contain elements
- Wrong: `.aceui-table--striped__row` ❌
- Right: `.aceui-table.aceui-table--striped` with `.aceui-table__row` inside ✅

### Combining modifiers
- Never chain modifiers: `.aceui-button--primary--disabled` ❌
- Use multiple classes: `.aceui-button .aceui-button--primary .aceui-button--disabled` ✅

### Element names: structure, not appearance
- Wrong: `.aceui-modal__blueHeader`, `.aceui-modal__largeBody` (encodes visual style)
- Right: `.aceui-modal__header`, `.aceui-modal__body` ✅

### Do not use HTML tag names as elements
- Wrong: `.aceui-table__tr`, `.aceui-table__td` ❌
- Right: `.aceui-table__row`, `.aceui-table__cell` ✅

### State vs structure
- **Elements** = permanent parts: `__header`, `__body`, `__row`, `__cell`
- **Modifiers** = variants or temporary state: `--primary`, `--disabled`, `--loading`, `--active`

### JavaScript state classes
- For **JS-toggled DOM state** (open, active, expanded): use non-BEM utility classes so BEM is not tied to JS — e.g. `.is-open`, `.is-active`, `.has-error`.
- For **design variants** (primary, size, type): use BEM modifiers — e.g. `.aceui-button--primary`, `.aceui-modal--large`.

### When not to use BEM
- Utility classes (`.hidden`, `.text-center`)
- Layout helpers (`.grid`, `.flex`)
- Spacing helpers (`.mt-4`, `.gap-2`)
- BEM is for **component styling only**.

### Allowed vs disallowed
- **Allowed:** `.aceui-block`, `.aceui-block__element`, `.aceui-block--modifier`, `.aceui-block__element--modifier`
- **Disallowed:** modifier chaining, nested elements, mixing structure with state, encoding visual styles in names

## Class Naming Rules

- Always use lowercase letters; multi-word with single hyphen (kebab-case)
- No camelCase or underscores in class names: `.aceui-notification__close-button` ✅ not `__closeButton` or `__close_button`
- Use `__` for element relationships, `--` for modifiers
- Avoid abbreviations unless very common (e.g. `btn` ok; prefer `dropdown` not `dd`)
- Be descriptive: `.aceui-nav__menu-item` not `.aceui-nav__nmi`

## Class Application

- Base class first: `className={\`aceui-button ${className}\`.trim()}`
- Modifiers conditionally: `className={\`aceui-button ${isPrimary ? 'aceui-button--primary' : ''} ${className}\`.trim()}`
- External classes last: append `className` prop to the end of the class string
- Use string class names with `aceui-` prefix (e.g. `'aceui-button'`, `'aceui-button--primary'`)

## Avoid

- camelCase (`.primaryButton` ❌)
- Single underscore (`.button_icon` ❌)
- Generic classes (`.active`, `.large` ❌)
- Abbreviations (`.btn-prm` ❌)
